     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "A shopkeeper sold pencils at 3 rupees and erasers at 2 rupees.\n\"I can write the total as 3p + 2e,\" he said."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "like terms",
     "simplify",
     "model"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "We model real situations using letter-numbers. If p pencils and e erasers are bought, the cost is 3p plus 2e.\nWe omit the multiplication sign: 3p means 3 times p. Like terms have the same letter and can be combined: 3p plus 5p is 8p. Unlike terms cannot be combined.\nTo simplify 2n plus 3 plus 4n minus 1, group like terms: 6n plus 2."
    }
   },
